  "finalText": "## Summary\n\nI have cancelled reservation R3311 and settled it according to airline rules. **However, Marcus is receiving $248 in travel credit, not a cash refund to his card—here's why:**\n\n**The refund rules state:**\n- Trip insurance **does not provide cash refunds** for cancellations made within 14 days of departure\n- Marcus cancelled only 8 days before his 2026-08-05 departure\n- Therefore, per Rule 3 of the refund policy, the trip insurance converts the $248 fare into **travel credit** instead of returning it to the card\n- The $50 cancellation service fee is **waived** because Marcus holds platinum frequent-flyer status\n\n**What Marcus gets:**\n- ✅ $248.00 in travel credit (for future flights)\n- ✅ No cancellation service fee charged\n- ✗ No cash back to his card (trip insurance window requires 14+ days before departure)\n\n**Ledger entry:** Travel credit of $248.00 issued via L1\n\nMarcus needs to be informed that while his trip insurance protects his booking, it only provides cash refunds if the cancellation is made at least 14 days before departure. His credit can be used for future travel with the airline.",
